rule order_cancels_everything v1
description "The same order as order_happens, with a table that does nothing useful: every event cancels it. No `never` or `once` line minds, so `check` finds no error, and only warnings say the other states are not reached. Add `possible delivered` and it stops with E146."

enum order_state = received | paid | shipped | delivered | cancelled
enum happening = pay | ship | deliver | cancel

inputs
  state : order_state
  event : happening

outputs
  next_state : order_state
  refund     : money[JPY]  round down(1JPY)

table step
policy unique
| state     | event | -> next_state | refund |
| received  | -     | cancelled     | 0JPY   |
| paid      | -     | cancelled     | 0JPY   |
| shipped   | -     | cancelled     | 0JPY   |
| delivered | -     | state         | 0JPY   |
| cancelled | -     | state         | 0JPY   |

machine order over step
  carry   state -> next_state
  initial received
  final   delivered, cancelled
  never   shipped after cancelled
  once    refund >0JPY
